			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize Utility error mapping and security into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Utility` module in the Environment provider by removing public re-exports that violated the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. Extract logical units into dedicated submodules: `ErrorMapping` for `MapApplicationStateLockErrorToCommonError` and `UriParsing` for URI-to-URL conversion logic, while consolidating path validation into `PathSecurity`.\n\nUpdate all 26+ Environment provider implementations (Command, Configuration, Diagnostic, Document, FileSystem, and others) to call these utilities via their explicit full paths (`Utility::ErrorMapping::Fn`, `Utility::UriParsing::Fn`, `Utility::PathSecurity::Fn`) rather than through the flat namespace. This structural refactor eliminates implicit imports, enforces strict PascalCase function naming across the codebase, and establishes a consistent, atomic namespace hierarchy for future utility expansion.",
			"SHA": "b72100dc594a09915d480112e7d77972a5b18794"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
