				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				907,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize ExtensionManagement into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `ExtensionManagement` module documentation and inline logic into a dedicated submodule tree to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. The previous 36-line documentation-heavy file has been replaced with a concise surface exposing `Scanner` for extension discovery and `VsixInstaller` for VSIX archive installation.\n\nThis structural refactor extracts the extension lifecycle responsibilities (scanning bundled/user trees, manifest parsing, and installation) into atomic units while preserving the architectural contract where Mountain handles discovery and Cocoon handles activation over gRPC. This establishes a consistent namespace hierarchy for future expansion of marketplace integration and dependency resolution.",
			"SHA": "2c79a79125add2497b79c76b23436ca1e09468be"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T00:57:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				907,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize Telemetry module into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic Telemetry module documentation and inline functions into a dedicated submodule tree to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. Extract compile-time gate checks (`IsDebugBuild`, `IsDevelopmentBuild`, `IsEnabled`) and the initialization logic (`Initialize`) into separate files. The `mod.rs` is reduced from a large documentation-heavy file to a concise surface exposing the `Gates`, `Tracing`, `Metrics`, `FeatureFlags`, and `Initialize` submodules.\n\nThis structural refactor preserves all existing feature-gating logic and conditional compilation behavior while establishing a consistent namespace hierarchy for the upcoming wiring of the OpenTelemetry stack in `Binary::Main`.",
			"SHA": "b029f3c0da76428d66ad88fb0f8983fa7e824c22"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
