				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				903,
				12
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize RunTime execute and shutdown into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Execute` and `Shutdown` modules within `Source/RunTime` into dedicated submodule trees to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention and improve modularity. The `Execute` logic is split into `Run`, `RunWithRetry`, and `RunWithTimeout` files, while `Shutdown` is divided into `DisposeTerminalsSafely`, `FlushPendingOperations`, `SaveApplicationState`, `ShutdownCocoonWithRetry`, and `ShutdownWithRecovery`.\n\nExtract the `ApplicationRunTime` implementation blocks from the previous single-file `Fn.rs` and `Shutdown.rs` structures into their own files. Update `mod.rs` files to expose these new atomic units. The `ShutdownCocoonWithRetry` logic retains the critical \"Atom I6\" hard-kill fallback to prevent EADDRINUSE errors on restart, now isolated in its own module.\n\nThis structural refactor preserves all runtime behavior for effect execution (Echo scheduler integration, timeouts, retries) and graceful shutdown sequencing while establishing a consistent namespace hierarchy for future lifecycle feature expansion.",
			"SHA": "a4c9b57c6d1ebe9e14d1f4cef7361df1b3730845"
		}
